- Story & Context: High atop the salt-crystal ridge of Jebel-Krona, caravan lore tells of an ancient junk truck carrying fifty thousand quartz watch movements that overturned during a midsummer heatwave and fused permanently with the rock bed. Whenever the solstice wind rips across the peak at eighty miles per hour, the vibrating crystals trigger the acoustic resonators of abandoned wooden xylophones left by passing troupes, producing a blinding, lemon-flavored static that makes entire herds of pack animals trot in perfect four-four synchronization. As soaring analog synth leads blend with the howling natural frequencies of the stones, travelers gather along the ridge to dance, shouting the legendary caravan refrain, "The seasons cannot catch what the battery never counted!" until the sun dips behind the dune line.
